{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790979784,"nonce":"Y9kPzNkPfmh7FmsfkvR8dmAF6P0=","message":"Landed as `tui: a gantt row with no start draws its band from today (04248c5)`, on the same branch as f4426ff and f9c991e.\n\nWhat it draws now:\n\n- **No start, a stop ahead**: nothing before today, the dull band from today's period, then the stop's trail fading left into it. The weeks already gone by are no longer painted as weeks the work might have been done in.\n- **No dates at all**: the band from today's period to the chart's right edge.\n- **No start, a stop already past**: the stop keeps its marker — the six-cell trail fading left — and a short band runs from the stop to today, in the overdue tint. Nothing is drawn past such a stop.\n- **A start and no stop**: unchanged, fading from its start to the right and running on as the band to the chart's edge.\n\n**The tint, my call as you left it**: red (`lipgloss.Color(\"1\")`), at full strength rather than the dull blend a normal band gets, and it outranks the group's tint. A date already missed is what the eye is on a chart for, and the group is readable from the row's neighbours; a grabbed bar keeps the grab's yellow, since that is the state the keys are in. Recorded in `gantt_view.go` (`overdueTint`) and in the design doc.\n\n**`extent`** counts a missing start as today, so a stop-only row sizes the chart to today-to-stop rather than to the point its stop is. The knock-on, worth naming: a dateless parent whose only dated child is a stop-only row now draws its envelope over today-to-stop too, which is what that child draws. A parent whose children have both dates is unchanged. The milestone trail no longer reads its period off `extent` — `milestoneCol` gives the row's own date — so the wider extent does not move the marker.\n\n`nowCol()` is new because `index()` clamps a date past the chart to its last period, which is right for a cursor and wrong for a band: without it a chart that ends before today would draw the band on its last period instead of not at all. `nowCol` answers -1 before the chart and `len(periods)` after.\n\nTests in `tui/gantt_test.go`: `TestGanttARowWithNoStartBandsFromToday` covers the three cases and the extent, with `today` fixed at 2026-09-28 as the others do; `TestGanttMilestonesAndDatelessRows` and `TestGanttMilestonesTrailAwayFromTheirDate` were updated — the latter's `ends` row has its stop in today's own period, so the band before the trail is correctly gone. The Gantt section of the design doc and the AGENTS.md gantt sentence say all of this.","files":null}]}